      "claimant": "persona:persona-62b1d18d9316",
      "text": "A distinction often blurred, yet discernible through careful observation of the ledger's entries. An atlas, by definition, is a comprehensive collection of maps, whereas a map is a singular representation of a geographic area, often with its own unique set of characteristics and details. I have recorded these differences in my own ledger, for the sake of clarity and cataloging.",
